simplybs: only give up early on failed mirror lookups.

simplybs fetches sources via ftpmirror.gnu.org, which load-balances to random
mirrors that occasionally 403/time out. Its download loop aborts on the first
0-byte response instead of using its own 15-retry loop, so a single bad mirror
kills the whole build. Limit that early give-up to mirror lookups (isMirror),
so the origin URL keeps retrying through the redirect roulette until it lands
on a working mirror.

--- a/simplybs/utils/download/download.go
+++ b/simplybs/utils/download/download.go
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 		bytesReceived, err := downloadWithResume(path, url, expectedSha256)
 		if err != nil {
 			// If no data was received on first try, give up immediately
-			if bytesReceived == 0 && attempt == 0 {
+			if bytesReceived == 0 && attempt == 0 && isMirror {
 				return fmt.Errorf("no data received from server: %v", err)
 			}
 			if attempt == maxRetries {
